1. Anchore prior-art (syft + grype) — Apache-2.0
================================================================

Project: anchore/syft
Source: https://github.com/anchore/syft
License: Apache License, Version 2.0
Audited at: docs/adr/0001-prior-art-audit.md (2026-05-19)

Project: anchore/grype
Source: https://github.com/anchore/grype
License: Apache License, Version 2.0
Audited at: docs/adr/0001-prior-art-audit.md (2026-05-19)

Adoption shape (per ADR-0001 §"Adoption shape"): REFERENCE-ONLY at
the design layer. No syft or grype source code is vendored or
copied verbatim. The TypeScript implementation under src/ was
written from scratch.

The following modules were INFORMED BY (not derived from) syft /
grype design study during Stage 1.5 prior-art audit:

  - src/parsers/                  SBOM-format manifest parsing
                                  patterns (pURL handling, license
                                  expression normalisation,
                                  dependency-edge classification)
                                  informed by syft.
  - src/emitters/spdx-2.3.ts      SPDX emission field-mapping
                                  conventions informed by syft.
  - src/emitters/cyclonedx-1.5.ts CycloneDX emission field-mapping
                                  + deterministic serialNumber
                                  derivation informed by syft.
  - src/scanners/correlator.ts    OSV advisory ↔ component
                                  correlation heuristics + range-
                                  event traversal informed by grype.
  - src/scanners/severity.ts      Severity normalisation +
                                  ranking conventions informed by
                                  grype.
  - src/util/credential-scrub.ts  Credential-pattern masking at the
                                  emitter boundary — direct lesson
                                  from CVE-2025-65965 (grype
                                  GHSA-6gxw-85q2-q646, registry
                                  credential disclosure to output
                                  file). The mitigation pattern is
                                  required by AC-NF-credentials.

Subprocess wrap (per ADR-0001 §"Adoption shape" + T-39): when a user
explicitly passes `--use-syft` or `--use-grype`, sbom-pilot spawns the
locally-installed Anchore binary and parses its stdout. The binary's
cosign signature must verify before spawn (AC-NF-cosign-gate);
otherwise sbom-pilot refuses with sysexits EX_NOPERM. The binary is
NOT distributed with sbom-pilot — the user is responsible for
installing it via the upstream Anchore-documented install path.

